Runtime worker: measured under the emulated P2, red then green.

MEASUREMENT: tools/sb_costs.c (new, with the target 'sandbox-costs' in mk/sandbox.mk) measures what the charged native work costs in VM instructions: the VM instruction is the budget's unit (the count hook charges HOOK_STRIDE units per stride instructions), so a factor is the measured time of one unit of native work divided by the measured time of one VM instruction. Runs on the host and under qemu-i386 -cpu pentium2 (i686 musl, -march=i686 -mno-sse -static).

Host and emulated target, five runs (the ranges include the run-to-run spread):
  element touched:  1 .. 7 instructions per element (concat 4 .. 7, unpack 1 .. 6)
  byte copied:      0.15 .. 0.6 instructions per byte
  byte parsed:      7 .. 24 instructions per byte (emulated median 14)
The host and the emulated target disagree by up to a factor of two; the emulated target (no SSE, like the P2) is the closer model, and the ratio is what survives the emulation - an absolute time here is only an upper bound.

RED: t/sandbox/test_sandbox.c got test_calibrated_charges(), which pins the calibrated charges (a concat over 100 elements = 800 units, a 1000 byte string copy = 501, a 1000 byte load = 16000) and checks the budget boundary: the charge is admitted, one unit less is refused. It failed with the old factors: 'concat one unit below its charge: got OK, want FAULT_BUDGET' (and the same for the string copy and the load).

FIX: include/canlin/sandbox_limits.h - CANLIN_SB_COST_ELEM 1 -> 8, CANLIN_SB_COST_BYTES_PER_UNIT 16 -> 2, CANLIN_SB_COST_LOAD_BYTE 1 -> 16 (each the round-up that keeps the charge at or above the measured cost). The comment now says for every value whether it is measured or set: the three factors are measured (ratio, canlin#13), the budgets (CANLIN_SB_BUDGET_DEFAULT, _DRAW), the hook stride and the pattern-match charge are set and unchanged - the P2's time per VM instruction is still unknown, so the spec's '100-200 ms on a P2' stays its estimate.

GREEN: sandbox: 331 checks passed; host make BUILD=build/rt3 test - 23 suites, ALL TESTS PASSED (the UI and LLM charges use the same constants and still pass). i686 gate running.

Also: mk/sandbox.mk and mk/module.mk now list include/canlin/sandbox_limits.h as a prerequisite - without it a changed factor did not rebuild the objects that charge with it (found while making this change; the ui.mk and llm.mk lists still miss it, see the report).

